{start_of_verse}
[G]Got a home in the hills of old Virginia I love still
And it stands near the lonesome [D]pines
And I [G]long to go back to the vine covered shack
Where I left that old [D]mother of [G]mine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]I can still see her there in that old rocking chair
In my home among the [D]hills
And I [G]seem to hear her say why did you go away
From your home [D]among the [G]hills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]The pine trees stand alone near my old Virginia home
And that silver hared mother of [D]mine
I can [G]see her smiling face in that old familiar place
In my home [D]among the [G]hills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]I’m leaving here today I’m going back to stay
In my home among the [D]hills
How [G]happy we will be near the lonesome pine trees
In my home [D]among the [G]hills
{end_of_verse}
